error: `next` holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  `next` does `System.signalNext`
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_signals_next_in_async.sg:4:20
 4 |     print(listener.next())
   |                    ^^^^
  hint: `await listener.nextAsync()` does the same work without holding the thread
